# Every image builds from the repository root as its context, so anything not
# excluded here is shipped to the daemon and can be picked up by a COPY.
#
# This file did not exist, and its absence was not theoretical. The web image
# runs `npm ci` from the lockfile in one stage and then does `COPY apps/web ./`
# in the next, which silently overwrote that freshly installed tree with
# whatever `node_modules` happened to be lying on the build host. Production ran
# Next 16.2.11 from a July checkout while the lockfile said 16.3.0, so a
# dependency bump made specifically to clear three high advisories never reached
# production and nothing reported a problem.

# Version control and CI. Large, and never needed inside an image.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Installed dependency trees. The images install their own from a lockfile;
# copying a host tree in defeats the point of a reproducible build.
**/node_modules

# Build output. A stale local build must never be mistaken for a fresh one.
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
contracts/out
contracts/cache
contracts/lib

# Secrets. Nothing in the tree copies these today, but the cost of one careless
# `COPY . .` in future is the production environment file inside a shipped
# image layer.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Local state and caches.
backups
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/coverage
**/htmlcov
**/*.log

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Documentation. Read on GitHub, not from inside a container.
docs
*.md
LICENSE
